{:db/id 17592186179742 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id 17592186179604 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}] :question/id #uuid "d844a573-49a1-59c3-bec4-e409c486469d" :question/math-academy-id "e-9542" :question/problem "![](images/29/298b7b4293ff104a62107670fa2aba603b8a23e9ad042f7e270a4acf6267a2fa.png)\n\n \n\nConsider the vector field $\\mathbf F(x,y)$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path where the curve is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r <  0$\n\nII. $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r =         0$\n\nIII. $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r >  0$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r$ gives the total work done by a force $\\mathbf F$ in moving a particle along $C\\mathbin{:}$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r > 0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion  of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r <                     0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Since the force $\\mathbf F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/cd/cd71f379a02405bc21aecfb0bb14e9798cfbc4d7fd2c1d3a1d5221aa8d64638f.png)\n\n \nSo, $\\displaystyle\\int_C\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r = 0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $\\mathbf F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/b2/b2284e7ffa962fd46333c4eca47a77473007fdd96e0813b9928f0303df8170f3.png)\n\n \nSo, $\\displaystyle\\int_{-C}\\mathbf F\\cdot \\textrm d \\mathbf r = 0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id 17592186050885}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id 17592186180019 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "165abac8-b78d-5d8b-9797-98764bec8a25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186459473} {:answer/id #uuid "9682a02a-0b80-592c-b204-2e00e64c9de0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186459474}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "165abac8-b78d-5d8b-9797-98764bec8a25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186459473} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8082197-4ec5-5193-873e-90d47f00746b" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186460603} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e01fbca2-a092-5b1e-95d7-018e7d1f5edc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186459475} {:answer/id #uuid "5bd8e7a9-c801-5eeb-bd2b-c483bdb34b5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186459476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5bd8e7a9-c801-5eeb-bd2b-c483bdb34b5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186459476} :answer-field/id #uuid "422cd737-9b8c-53f2-a0cd-c12e1ad7286c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186460604} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7fbcc0ff-2235-56bb-aa08-904c6e3a229b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186459477} {:answer/id #uuid "b0c4988b-246a-5c24-99ad-02a2f31d8f3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186459478}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0c4988b-246a-5c24-99ad-02a2f31d8f3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186459478} :answer-field/id #uuid "07711a4e-3e3f-5c90-b74e-ec28eded9fbf" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186460605}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "58d69dfd-31b1-5851-b7cd-9ea022ec672e" :question/math-academy-id "q-125380" :question/problem "![](images/14/145b9dcc1e52dec65d64245afa89fba77e0d0cda5a919b52009e2397f3f03e16.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the segment $\\overset{―}{AB}$ traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion  of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/20/20121d30445c9e756f1c2c024713bc6cd6f0464cfcfc24df68bc30c766c4988e.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/0f/0ff98536c275458d68deabda91f56bf63e7c8f59f5ea79c68292332d8cd58d4f.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id 17592186180020 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "47df525a-0d27-5474-842e-e797864d924f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186459479} {:answer/id #uuid "0f4b12aa-dfc8-5cf6-bb46-fa30cda83363" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186459480}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "47df525a-0d27-5474-842e-e797864d924f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186459479} :answer-field/id #uuid "3ebe448c-6d78-52eb-b87a-c0f6378a526d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186460606} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b3a5163-4335-5da1-a308-4afc6fa83343" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186459481} {:answer/id #uuid "2865bf65-f4fa-5527-9338-dac5b94be08d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186459482}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2865bf65-f4fa-5527-9338-dac5b94be08d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186459482} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a6785c8-4fa8-5419-98ef-b6ca891fd2fe" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186460607} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4a7f457e-5e87-5921-9c97-354280faa2c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186459483} {:answer/id #uuid "58d82791-fb0b-511f-a411-3a2ed07c51ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186459484}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "58d82791-fb0b-511f-a411-3a2ed07c51ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186459484} :answer-field/id #uuid "5480c90b-6e84-5672-a102-83d8323aaae1" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186460608}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "26c0cce0-6deb-59c6-a9c4-06e4698080d8" :question/math-academy-id "q-125381" :question/problem "![](images/50/501a3512fb4b8a1898c6dfb8816d587de4a0cd585991d9c92d2bb35d83a2853d.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the semicircle is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/4c/4c11b38f9e598e0cd8fc50715d2091e5bea48d188440ae8a99c84d66a6acb6b9.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/34/346007ae582fccdf4519a3d1cd50a467e19d5345238343a1311fd3348bbeb138.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id 17592186259817 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25c37202-f845-5fe8-8a7a-1db1f298b82f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463464} {:answer/id #uuid "814c544b-ea3b-5e5e-85a8-e01671b5faa5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463465}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "25c37202-f845-5fe8-8a7a-1db1f298b82f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463464} :answer-field/id #uuid "72d39b77-fe29-5793-a0fb-0f2c0ded2a24" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186464666} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "66c009aa-e253-537e-b9ea-d64ce314b9a8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463466} {:answer/id #uuid "ee7535b0-5862-5dfa-963f-9d8f8799fc40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463467}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee7535b0-5862-5dfa-963f-9d8f8799fc40" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463467} :answer-field/id #uuid "401ef778-f261-5f37-b35b-442681079175" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186464667} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fe4ca179-59d3-5f0e-a769-a1d46a8dd48d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463468} {:answer/id #uuid "2ae8df09-8879-50b4-8407-98178c0cb9e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463469}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fe4ca179-59d3-5f0e-a769-a1d46a8dd48d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463468} :answer-field/id #uuid "ecf5381b-d126-5634-9a8c-5944ea06f42d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186464668}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0ce534ad-d76e-5678-87a2-87c2bbfd4370" :question/math-academy-id "q-125500" :question/problem "![](images/8d/8dc3102ab0055d4e7dde7c79873a2c3d825fa9c803ea1ee2376a7dbe920c5535.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path where the quarter circle is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion  of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/ac/ac9d8388e73a33df98ac7f04fe161ae75b27b4b01a79213c07e10d43c328d747.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/92/92e6f3ca98d7adbb34765307c0c570f55ce85f7f10cf6bef28bdb93d68a0c1cb.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id 17592186259818 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1cfa6683-6722-5eeb-96a9-3db5e8cf9923" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463470} {:answer/id #uuid "75906f44-44f3-5c13-92f4-cc5703a4776e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463471}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1cfa6683-6722-5eeb-96a9-3db5e8cf9923" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463470} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8d2d0d3-81db-50eb-a9fb-a003de2f2449" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186464669} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4736c250-e772-5723-98dc-f93776c74c93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463472} {:answer/id #uuid "fca386ca-2828-5d6c-9232-724a2e7d32ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463473}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fca386ca-2828-5d6c-9232-724a2e7d32ef" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463473} :answer-field/id #uuid "63e272b7-517f-5dd8-b86c-d72d0456faf3" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186464670} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e6a6e849-4c6b-52a5-b5eb-bf0993666973" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463474} {:answer/id #uuid "7c6c0bcb-c01b-55d2-88c8-5dd7ed78b8a6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e6a6e849-4c6b-52a5-b5eb-bf0993666973" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463474} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec32f74a-0dc2-5daf-8e33-34c8db66e97a" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186464671}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "eb3b3139-68a2-57de-b20c-f84dd8321120" :question/math-academy-id "q-125501" :question/problem "![](images/ee/ee674d6140d9326894d607ca9a3feede580ce68bd56ca762a013a9602a657832.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path where the curve is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion  of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/d6/d69e4c3dee5a346baae0accffc4d234b5b84e0402d107b5d1a24160a796992dd.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/61/61a1ebee96c7082485b318d5bcc1f55a42c0f4589b0aad9edf09e4deb82a2403.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id 17592186259819 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6b904a0b-0910-5626-8d87-2d88fb8897f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463476} {:answer/id #uuid "ca7170fa-1276-577a-8d37-143e3bc54016" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463477}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6b904a0b-0910-5626-8d87-2d88fb8897f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463476} :answer-field/id #uuid "813913cc-5007-5f69-a965-673ce565c158" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186464672} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07e328df-cc3b-5f1a-a1c7-d827c0da6c08" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463478} {:answer/id #uuid "4873fd1a-fd38-5b50-92b1-eb49a4809f49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463479}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4873fd1a-fd38-5b50-92b1-eb49a4809f49" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463479} :answer-field/id #uuid "102c7b22-3f98-5961-8442-de712d1fdb0a" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186464673} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "61ea1c46-99e9-5c3f-9e8e-02791213ab6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463480} {:answer/id #uuid "df377ce9-8b4b-5523-b521-fd4d8b80b6ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463481}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "61ea1c46-99e9-5c3f-9e8e-02791213ab6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463480} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b28deb9-6649-5aa3-a4aa-0d6353b676e5" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186464674}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2e7b4d84-452a-51cd-8b75-fc51fa3ff9bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-125504" :question/problem "![](images/97/97f1287fa4c3662c070914e4cc93879cebaa72b07e2b2b5c03143941c647ed11.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above, and let $C$ be the path along the quarter circle traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion  of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false, while statement II is true. Since the force $F$ acts perpendicular to the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B,$ it neither helps nor hinders its motion. \n\n![](images/e0/e07fca985a11d4edb66ea91d9a560ab134d81f5f20aaba8b376677d0de2dd3e7.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\n- Statement III is false. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/78/78de6ce0133bec33c14eabb43db2e53eb8d76653aa1fc121c83f47c4b91c3b94.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""} {:db/id 17592186259820 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "831cb1b1-064e-559a-8090-c5ef5904d2b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463482} {:answer/id #uuid "f119cf42-93c5-5b60-9a16-92306e80bd8f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463483}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "831cb1b1-064e-559a-8090-c5ef5904d2b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463482} :answer-field/id #uuid "069a4e64-f502-58b7-afe8-73851d7f80b9" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186464675} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a59c28f9-7a4d-56a4-8b36-20c269b2a473" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463484} {:answer/id #uuid "984ca6d5-aa97-5d84-8ae3-06c8f43e8370" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463485}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "984ca6d5-aa97-5d84-8ae3-06c8f43e8370" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463485} :answer-field/id #uuid "5285b4f0-a29a-5753-9eed-ad304e29d4c6" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186464676} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3250d354-20d6-54d0-97fb-d9ecc4f3e804" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463486} {:answer/id #uuid "e358fd30-0443-5b9f-be75-140d1a5f4544" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e358fd30-0443-5b9f-be75-140d1a5f4544" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463487} :answer-field/id #uuid "c43a9049-f742-5536-9ca5-222ebee9078f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186464677}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "91c88aa7-9c4e-5dd7-9c30-608f94c03554" :question/math-academy-id "q-125507" :question/problem "![](images/86/866a1812bd31e0443becf35a7cc2b8df1bc84a49091a94250b60fe3533e4b172.png)\n\nConsider the vector field $F(x,y)$ shown above. Let $C$ be the path where the semiellipse is traversed from $A$ to $B.$ Which of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n- ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0$\n- ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "Remember that ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r$ gives the total work done by a force $F$ in moving a particle along $C:$\n\n- If the force works *with* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force helps to push the particle along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\n- If the force works *against* the motion of the particle (i.e., the force impedes the motion of the particle as it moves along the path), then ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's check each statement.\n\n- Statement I is false while statement II is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ works against the motion of the particle as it moves from $A$ to $B.$\n\n![](images/e4/e4232577b0687d781f702a196ae2c0060d3264c1f44a45a404a0f9da03bc0dd1.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r<0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. It's clear from the picture below that $F$ assists the motion of the particle as it moves from $B$ to $A.$\n\n![](images/f7/f7cfcef37ed6a52d5bd374fae2d7a00c4d8012e9ea8dbef43165c10bcc9471be.png)\n\nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r>0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id 17592186259844 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b9c996c-5a73-566e-bbb7-6b0823547575" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463530} {:answer/id #uuid "30a2656e-d4ea-5f17-9193-df6e7c38a132" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463531}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9b9c996c-5a73-566e-bbb7-6b0823547575" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463530} :answer-field/id #uuid "d493a8c4-7d2e-51cc-ac4a-a63d54af6e3d" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186464699} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4919df2b-1781-51fe-810e-b5fcd6350e48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id 17592186463532} {:answer/id #uuid "ae069756-d16c-5e63-af48-f69f18b462c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463533}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae069756-d16c-5e63-af48-f69f18b462c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id 17592186463533} :answer-field/id #uuid "d91f3df4-dbea-5df3-a3ae-7785cf6bf841" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id 17592186464700} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "98296909-a163-589b-af22-9510086818fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.typ