f32eb9e091f56f76ac3616cbb1cd81d5d212a86.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\n- Statement III is true. If we reverse the orientation of $C,$ then the situation with regards to the work done by $F$ is similar to the previous case.\n\n![](images/17/17423916013677c1476df5a4368ab9eec81671b04b4ca29a0e702b20ddc818f2.png)\n\n \nSo, ${\\int }_{-C}F\\cdot \\text{d}r=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\""} {:db/id 17592186551240 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3d72127a-90d6-5f7e-bd87-75d03285a918" :knowledge-point/title "Interpreting the Sign of a Line Integral Over a Non-Constant Vector Field"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ac92f55-bdd5-5ebb-8623-7211f79f9620" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186550395} {:answer/id #uuid "179b5f9d-873a-571a-b6bf-69376a9ef389" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id 17592186550418} {:answer/id #uuid "1dfb5464-e95f-5d2a-b797-775d6cf22682" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id 17592186550431} {:answer/id #uuid "a8026852-ad3d-5420-9b64-1828b556006e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id 17592186550811} {:answer/id #uuid "d9563607-dd70-5767-87cb-3d112f17eed5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id 17592186550956}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0ac92f55-bdd5-5ebb-8623-7211f79f9620" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id 17592186550395} :answer-field/id #uuid "be155506-4e79-5a1a-866f-997f1cb30ccc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id 17592186551181}] :question/difficulty {:db/id 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "17a8497e-763c-5804-a8ea-e63d106be3fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-125497" :question/problem "![](ima